{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"The sidebar is the navigation for every mode: History shows the ref list alone; Files and Changes show ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"RefBannerView","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" over the mode's section (tree, or the Changes list and commit box). What the banner says comes from ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"BranchBanner","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" (RcGitKit) and nowhere else. Views are hidden through ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"detachesHiddenViews","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", and AppKit drops an ancestor's constraints for a detached view for good, so a section carries no constraint to anything outside itself — size it with hugging.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":"bullet"},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"A view the stack has never laid out while attached gets no alignment constraint either, and unhiding does not backfill one: anything added or hidden before the first layout (a section, the ref list on a window that opens on Files, the truncation note) sizes to its content, so ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"show","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" re-makes the width of every view showing by hand (","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"docs/solutions/ui-bugs/nsstackview-hidden-at-attach-never-gets-width-alignment.md","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":").","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":"bullet"},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"In Files the ref list lives in ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"RefPickerController","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", a transient popover under the banner over the same ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"RefsViewController","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" in its ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":".picker","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" behavior: selection only highlights, a click or Return picks. Actions that ask with a sheet close the popover first. The banner opens it on mouse-down, and a transient popover closes on that same mouse-down when it is already open, so ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"chooseRef","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" ignores the event whose timestamp closed it. In Changes the banner is read-only: it names the checked-out branch through ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"BranchBanner.checkedOut","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", because Changes always compares the working tree with HEAD, and ⌘B is disabled there (","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"canOpenRefPicker","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":").","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":"bullet"},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"The sidebar collapses with ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":".preferResizingSiblingsWithFixedSplitView","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", so the window keeps its size; ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":".preferResizingSplitViewWithFixedSiblings","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" shrinks the window instead. The toolbar carries no ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":".sidebarTrackingSeparator","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":": ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"outerSplit","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" sits inside ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"DropHostViewController","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" rather than being the window's content controller, and a separator that cannot measure its split throws the items after it across the titlebar on collapse.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":"bullet"},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"A cell whose label carries an ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"NSAttributedString","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" puts its truncation in the string's ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":".paragraphStyle","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"; ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"lineBreakMode","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" on the field only applies to a plain ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"stringValue","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" and the text clips with no ellipsis. Keep a row's controls in one ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"NSTableCellView","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" on ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"centerYAnchor","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" rather than in separate table columns (","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"docs/solutions/ui-bugs/attributed-string-label-ignores-cell-linebreakmode.md","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":").","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":"bullet"},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"The Changes list is one ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"NSOutlineView","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" serving both groupings from ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"ChangeTree","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" (RcGitKit, pure and tested); flat rows are childless roots. Node identity dies on every reload, so expansion and selection are restored by ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"ChangeNode.key","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", never by row index or ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"path","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" (a file and a folder can share one path).","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":"bullet"},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"The file pane uses a TextKit 1 stack with ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"allowsNonContiguousLayout","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" and no wrapping; ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"LineNumberRulerView","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" numbers only fragments that begin a line, so a wrapped continuation gets no number. Wrapping would leave gaps in the gutter, not shift it — the markdown preview mode wraps and hides the ruler. Syntax colors are temporary attributes applied per visible chunk; never add a layout- affecting attribute (font, paragraph style) through that path.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":"bullet"},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"Text positions are UTF-16 offsets into the decoded ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"String","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":". ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"TextDocument","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" maps them from the bytes when the core says the blob is valid UTF-8, and walks ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"text.utf16","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" only for lossy input: a U+FFFD replacement shifts every later offset, so bytes no longer map to it.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":"bullet"},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"The markdown preview is two halves: ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"MarkdownDocument.parse","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" (RcGitKit, pure, byte-level, tested) turns source into flat blocks and styled runs, and ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"MarkdownRenderer","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" (RcGitApp) decides how each block looks. A new syntax goes in the parser with a test; the renderer never re-reads the source. Both run off the main actor, like the plain paint.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":"bullet"},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"Tables are ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"NSTextTable","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" cells and blockquotes and code panels are ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"NSTextBlock","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"s carried in the paragraph style. Layout-affecting attributes are fine on that build path and never on the source-mode temporary-attribute path.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":"bullet"},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"An ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"NSTextBlock","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" that is not an ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"NSTextTableBlock","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" has no intrinsic width and lays out one glyph per line without one. Build every standalone block through ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"Theme.fullWidthBlock()","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", which sets ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"setContentWidth(100, type: .percentageValueType)","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" (","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"docs/solutions/ui-bugs/nstextblock-without-content-width-collapses.md","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":").","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":"bullet"},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"Check preview layout by measuring, not by launching: ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"NSTextStorage","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" + ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"NSLayoutManager","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" + a fixed-width ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"NSTextContainer","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", then walk ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"lineFragmentRect","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":". A block fragment far narrower than the container is a collapsed block.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":"bullet"},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"Every markdown link resolves through ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"MarkdownLinkTarget.resolve","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" against the pane's ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"repositoryPath","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":". Do not read a destination anywhere else: telling a repository path, a URL and a ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"#fragment","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" apart in one place is what keeps clicking, the context menu and \"Copy Link\" from disagreeing. A repository link opens through ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"BrowserModel.openPath","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", which walks one tree object per component. Its ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"#fragment","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" goes with it: the model keeps it as ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"pendingReveal","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" only once the load starts, and the pane takes it after it paints. A content-search match travels the same way (","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"openContentMatch","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"). Never hold a reveal in the view — a dead link would leave it for the next file to scroll to.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":"bullet"},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"Import links in source mode never enter the text storage: ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"LinkTextView","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" asks its owner which range a character falls in and draws the hover underline as a temporary attribute. A ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":".link","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" attribute would be a storage edit, which invalidates layout for every range it touches. Links load on the first pointer move (","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"FileViewController.importLink(at:)","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"), and a click resolves through ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"BrowserModel.openImport","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" and ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"ImportResolver","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" — never resolve a specifier in a view, and never keep a resolved path: the tree on screen decides.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":"bullet"},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"In ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"MainWindowController.init","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", views are built before ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"setFrameUsingName","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":": the frame restore resizes the window and fires ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"windowDidResize","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" -> ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"applyLayout()","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" synchronously, and an exception there is swallowed by launch Apple Event handling, leaving the app windowless (","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"docs/solutions/runtime-errors/appkit-swallowed-launch-exception-windowless-app.md","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"). Keep delegate callbacks safe during construction: ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":".first","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", not ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"[0]","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":".","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":"bullet"},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"Every sidebar list goes through ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"Style.sidebarList","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" (a source list whose rows follow the system sidebar size) and every icon-and-label row is a ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"SidebarCellView","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"; anything above a list keeps ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"Style.margin","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" so it lines up with the selection.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":"bullet"},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"Never set a per-row font on a plain-string ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"textField","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" outlet: in any table whose ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"rowSizeStyle","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" is not ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":".custom","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", AppKit re-applies a plain system font to that outlet at every layout. Use an attributed string, ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":".custom","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" row size, or a label that is not the outlet — as ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"SidebarCellView","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" does, whose tables answer type-select through their delegate (","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"docs/solutions/ui-bugs/nstablecellview-textfield-outlet-font-reset-at-layout.md","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":").","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":"bullet"},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"Icons are SF Symbols from ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"Icons","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", tinted by the source list through ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"Icons.tint(for:)","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":". Never use ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"NSWorkspace","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" document icons: their colors come from whichever app claims the extension, and they clash with the tinted symbols beside them.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":"bullet"},
